5194-9f28-4bf3586b17c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371401 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that if  $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of a $3\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ then\n\n- $Σ$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix with nonnegative elements on the main diagonal and zeroes outside the main diagonal,\n\n- $U$ is an orthogonal $3\\times 3$ matrix,\n\n- $V$ is an orthogonal $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=3$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=1.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-9I & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]-9[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -4 \\\\ -4 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-9I)v=0$ gives the unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-1I & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-1I)v=0$ gives the unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrix $V:$\n\n$$\nV=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371402 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371403 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371402 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371402 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371405 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371402 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371406 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371402 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371407 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371402 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371402 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371402 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186371405 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371402 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "22a2cd66-5307-5558-babf-c76da5f3a89d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371403 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371403 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371403 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "14a0021b-af2d-542a-b89a-d1517e53d92a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371404 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371404 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371404 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "83c5e2aa-24ad-5e20-8b95-be9f2c895314" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371405 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371405 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371405 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aafebe45-27bc-5c92-97bc-57c0cf